# Build context exclusions.
#
# WHY every directory pattern is `**/`-prefixed: a `.dockerignore` pattern is matched against the
# path relative to the context root, so a bare `dist` excludes only the root `dist` and leaves
# `apps/*/dist` and `packages/*/dist` in the context. That was the previous behaviour, and it was
# invisible until someone ran `nx run <app>:prune` locally before a build — the leftover
# `apps/*/dist/workspace_modules/@private-cloud/*` directories then entered the image, where Nx
# found two projects claiming the same name and refused to build anything.
#
# The same applies to `node_modules`: nested ones were being copied into every build context.
.git
.github
**/.nx
**/coverage
**/dist
**/out-tsc
**/node_modules
docs
proxmox-
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
.backup
*.log
